-- CRISCIKEE DEMO DATA - LOCAL DATABASE ONLY. NOT A MIGRATION. NEVER PRODUCTION.
--
-- worker/migrations/ runs against the live D1 on every deploy, which is why
-- 0125 seeds the four flavours (configuration) and NOT ONE review: fake
-- feedback in the production table is fake business data, and the dashboard
-- would report it as fact.
--
-- This file exists so the analytics can be SEEN before real tastings happen.
-- Apply it to a LOCAL database only:
--
--   cd worker
--   npx wrangler d1 migrations apply azoneofficial --local
--   npx wrangler d1 execute azoneofficial --local --file=../scratch/criscikee-demo.sql
--   npx wrangler dev
--
-- Every row is marked sentiment_reasons = 'demo data', so a demo row can
-- never be mistaken for a customer, and this one statement removes them all:
--
--   DELETE FROM criscikee_reviews WHERE sentiment_reasons = 'demo data';
--
-- 174 reviews across the four launch flavours, with deliberate structure so
-- the grids have something to show: BBQ leads among 18-24, Original among
-- 45+, Spicy loses the over-45s, Cheese has too few reviews to be ranked.

